FreeWnn source and patch provenance
===================================

This candidate no longer uses the Debian 1.1.1~a021+cvs20130302-8 source
base. The upstream source is the FreeWnn 1.1.1-a023 tarball imported as
1.1.1~a023 and recorded by reference/a023-base. The historical Debian
packaging VCS through revision -5 is at reference/debian-packaging-2015;
the imported -8 packaging is at debian/1.1.1_a021+cvs20130302-8. The GCC
14/15 and C23 compatibility work is at reference/gcc15-main-20260711.

Historical Debian patch disposition
------------------------------------

* newlayout was empty and is dropped.
* makerules.mk.in is replaced by 1000-debian-filesystem-layout.patch.
* man is split into 1001-fix-manpage-sections.patch and
  1002-escape-hyphen-in-atod-manpage.patch.
* hardening-flags is dropped because a023 propagates CPPFLAGS and LDFLAGS.
* hurd_support.patch is refreshed as 0050-define-MAXPATHLEN-fallback.patch.
* fix-parallel-build.patch is dropped because a023 has the fixed dependency.
* egrep-a.patch is superseded by
  0005-build-dictionaries-in-C-locale.patch.
* implicit_functions.diff from -8 is replaced by the logical configure,
  system-declaration, and prototype patches in this series.

The patch-relevant -5 to -8 delta was: two DEP-3 fields added to
egrep-a.patch; implicit_functions.diff added for Debian bug #1065772; and
its series entry added. Other packaging changes are outside this task.

Mixed source commit mapping
---------------------------

* a85b88729c2fa7d0a2ec542d737c5e19061c8a47: sort callbacks -> 0020;
  jl_dic_add_e handlers -> 0022.
* 17578cf34877cad67c465335afbf499b88cecce1: getopt -> 0011; redundant
  bdic declarations -> 0012.
* 915ecd5efe7a9ab09fc073c8131687184a45dfa4: internal sort interface ->
  0020; direct qsort comparators -> 0021; jl_dic_add_e callbacks -> 0022;
  other internal callbacks -> 0023; byte-buffer types -> 0025.
* 9618769b8e758f537db180a9389c7ce10c536163: redundant declarations ->
  0012; internal helpers -> 0023; signal handlers -> 0030; variadic out ->
  0031.
* 3cc4bf1f5fd9178741dd904612f2110a9470e86b: byte-buffer signedness ->
  0025; the functional wnn_sStrncpy conversion-direction fix -> 0040.

The GCC reference also removes redundant jutil declarations in
4cf1f77f2e20b8540aaf8e9478ba6e440dff2a78. They have the exact purpose of
0012 and are recorded there to preserve the verified GCC reference tree.

Generated configure policy
--------------------------

Only configure.in changes are carried. Generated configure is excluded,
including d2ce32b7afd3d79e810c08051c937106cbdf1332 and the configure half of
b8c95ad64da5de58857c72f4b3644d90c6e6e53c. Regenerate it with autoreconf.

Testing
-------

The Debian build runs autoreconf through dh-autoreconf before configure.
Generated `configure` is deliberately absent from the quilt series.

The upstream clients use translated message-catalog entries as format
strings. Debian's format-security diagnostics remain enabled, but
`-Wno-error=format-security` keeps those legacy uses non-fatal. Converting
them safely requires auditing each catalog entry and all language variants;
it is documented as maintainer work rather than folded into the fixed C
portability patch series.

The full client build also retains a few implicit cross-file helper calls and
old callback pointer types outside the server/library portability scope of the
fixed patch series. Their diagnostics remain visible but non-fatal via
`-Wno-error=implicit-function-declaration` and
`-Wno-error=incompatible-pointer-types`. This preserves the historical client
functionality while making the remaining audit explicit.

The configured installation owner remains `root`. During the rootless Debian
staging install, `debian/rules` overrides `WNNOWNER` with the invoking build
user so upstream install rules do not attempt a privileged `chown`; dpkg's
package assembly records the shipped files with normal root ownership.
Some dictionaries are installed read-only before upstream `wnntouch` updates
their internal identifier. `debian/scripts/wnntouch-staging` grants owner
write access only for that update and restores the read-only mode afterward.

The `uum` client remains built, but its obsolete utmp writer and setgid mode
are disabled. This permits an accurate rootless build and avoids granting a
legacy terminal client privileges solely for login-accounting records; input
method functionality is unaffected.

`debian/tests/libwnn-smoke` compiles, links, and executes a small program
using the installed public `wnn/jllib.h` header and shared library.
`debian/tests/dictionary-locales` rebuilds all four language dictionary
directories under the C locale and an available UTF-8 locale, then compares
sorted manifests containing each generated file's relative pathname and
SHA-256 content hash. Any pathname or content difference fails the test. Both
scripts are deterministic CI helpers rather
than autopkgtests: the dictionary check needs the configured build tree and
build-only generators, while the library test is run explicitly after the
locally built packages have been installed.

Unresolved work
---------------

An adopter must select an appropriate Maintainer, complete copyright and
policy review, and decide how the existing init scripts should relate to
current init/systemd policy. These are upload blockers. The packaging does
not guess at that service-policy decision.

A jserver runtime test is not included. Installing and starting the current
server package creates system users, mutable dictionaries, init integration,
and persistent state; a test isolated from privileged ports and system state
needs a maintainer-approved service design first. Mule 1.1 compatibility has
not been tested.
